# Forge harness

- Workspace is the **super-repo**. Code lives in git submodules; agent memory lives in the **memory-repo** submodule at `.ai/memory/` (`memoryRoot = .ai/memory/<submodulePath>/`).
- **Board/SCM wins.** Memory is a projection. On discrepancy, update memory — do not "fix" the board to match memory.
- Every event/command starts with **resolve-paths** → **sync-memory** (pull memory-repo `origin/main`) → **resolve-config**. Path ambiguity or sync failure is a hard stop (`FORGE_SUPER_REPO`, `--submodule`, missing `.ai/memory` submodule).
- Event commands are the parent: spawn listed agents as **propose-only** subagents; parent merges, HITLs, validates, then Applies (vendor/SCM first, then memory, then **commit-memory** push to memory-repo `main`).
- Memory-repo is agent-owned git: **no branches, no PRs/MRs** — commit and push `main` only. Subagents do not Apply, do not HITL, and do not mutate SCM unless executing parent-approved Apply steps.
- Doc templates: required H2s only; empty sections OK; no extra H2s; current state only.
- Orientation: run `/forge.help`. New project: ensure `.ai/memory` submodule → `/forge.init-project` → `/forge.roadmap-review` → `/forge.backlog-grooming` → `/forge.refinement` (see README New project path).
- Board path: **Grooming → Refinement** (Intention + AC) → **`/forge.refinement` → Ready** (self-contained issue body + `ai-ready` or `human-ready`). `/forge.implement-ticket` only takes Ready + `ai-ready`.
- Optional `/forge.sync-schedule` can mirror Weekly/Biweekly/Monthly rituals to Google Calendar reminders when MCP is available — not required; never auto-starts events.
- Tickets are actionable only — never create epic/umbrella issues; use a host milestone when grouping **5+** related tickets.
- Skill folder names are unique; see [docs/skill-naming.md](docs/skill-naming.md).
